<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian Worldwide Expl lists at premium.</title>
<headline>Australian Worldwide Expl lists at premium.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil and gas explorer Australian Worldwide Exploration NL made its debut on the Australian Stock Exchange at 58 cents per share, a 16-percent premium to its 50 cent issue price.</p>
<p>The issue of 40 million shares, underwriten by Macquarie Underwriting, raised A$20 million. The company has assets in Argentina and New Zealand as well as Australia.</p>
<p>By 3.15 p.m. (0515 GMT), Australian Worldwide Exploration shares were at 65 cents, having touched a high of 64 cents and a low of 50 cents.</p>
<p>--Walter Watson 61-2 9373 1810</p>
</text>
